First Author: Koritsánszky
Title: Shifting Determinants of Mortality Risk After Orthotopic Heart Transplantation Identified by Machine Learning
Source number: 65

Very short summary: This retrospective single-center study included 581 adolescent and adult orthotopic heart transplant recipients treated in Hungary between 2012 and 2024. Random forest models with nested five-fold cross-validation and SHAP interpretation predicted 30-day and 1-year mortality; the model using preoperative and postoperative variables achieved a 1-year AUC of 0.86 (95% CI 0.80–0.92), although the inclusion of postoperative variables with incompletely defined measurement timing creates substantial risk of bias.

