	•	Section 3 Comments/Quotes: Random forest models were developed separately for 30-day and 1-year all-cause mortality using either preoperative variables alone or all available preoperative and postoperative variables. A nested cross-validation design used a five-fold inner loop for hyperparameter optimization and a five-fold outer loop for feature selection, model selection, and performance evaluation. Feature selection retained 15–25 predictors. SHAP values quantified the magnitude and direction of predictor contributions, and the final ensemble comprised five classifiers trained on distinct outer folds.

